  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="20">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Northu">Northu</ref> 20</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="20" corresp="#wit-d">Gif man mid cirican mangie, bete be lahslite.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock" corresp="#wit-d">If anyone traffics with a church, he is to pay with <hi rend="italic">lahslit</hi>.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin" corresp="#wit-d">If anyone engages in trade with a church, he is to compensate for that with <hi rend="italic">lahslit</hi>.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Wenn jemand mit einer Kirche Handel treibt, büsse er durch Rechtsbruchbusse.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If anyone traffics in a church, let him atone with the fine for breach of law (lahslit).</ab>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares VI Atr 15.</note>
      </div>
    </body>
